# TF2003 QVM

TF2003 QVM is a maintained version of the Team Fortress mod for QuakeWorld. It builds the server-side game logic as `qwprogs.qvm` for MVDSV and other QuakeWorld servers with QVM support. This fork focuses on bug fixes, compatibility, and safe server-load optimizations without changing the core gameplay.

## Build on Linux

Install a C compiler, CMake, and Ninja. On Debian/Ubuntu:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install build-essential cmake ninja-build
cmake -S . -B _cmake/qvm -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build _cmake/qvm --target qvm
```

The generated files are `_cmake/qvm/qwprogs.qvm` and `_cmake/qvm/qwprogs.map`.

## Build on Windows (Visual Studio 2022)

Install the **Desktop development with C++** workload and the **C++ CMake tools for Windows** component. Open **Developer PowerShell for VS 2022** in the repository directory and run:

```powershell
cmake -S . -B _cmake/qvm_vs2022 -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build _cmake/qvm_vs2022 --target qvm
```

The generated files are `_cmake/qvm_vs2022/qwprogs.qvm` and `_cmake/qvm_vs2022/qwprogs.map`.

To install the mod, copy `qwprogs.qvm` to the server's `fortress` directory and run the server with QVM support enabled (for MVDSV, use `-progtype 3`).
